==== Opening the case ====
**Note:** This will void your warranty!

  *Remove the two visible screws on the upper part of the back of the case.
  *Remove the triangular pads on the lower part of the back of the case. There are two more screws under these pads, remove them too.
  *Open it carefully by introducing the tip of the screwdriver inside the division in the side of the case.

{{media:asus:rt-ac87u:rt-ac87u_case_back.jpg?direct&400|**Back of the case**}}

==== Hardware notes ====
As you can see in the following diagram, WAN/LAN2/LAN3/LAN4 ports are connected to BCM4709/BCM53012 and LAN1 is connected to QT3840BC/RTL8211E.\\
Both BCM4709/BCM53012 and QT3840BC/RTL8211E are connected through Port 5 by GMII. This is why Port 5 needs to be overriden.\\
{{media:asus:rt-ac87u:rt-ac87u_hardware.png?direct&600|}}\\
This hardware configuration has a side effect: LAN1 port isn't available unless Quantenna SoC is up and running.\\
In order to boot Quantenna SoC we have to provide a TFTP server with at least the U-Boot and Firmware files for the Quantenna.\\
Whenever our TFTP server is running on the BCM4709 with the required files we can set GPIO8 to output and high value in order to boot the Quantenna SoC.\\
Then the Quantenna SoC will boot from a minimal bootloader stored in its SPI flash and it will request the full U-Boot through TFTP.\\
Once U-Boot is running it will request the full firmware through TFTP.

